From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI power menu: white panel with an outline, no scrim

On the device (Test V40) the power menu's panel was grey 245 with no edge (the
theme's colorPrimaryDark; its elevation casts no shadow in software drawing),
and its window background was the wallpaper-coloured gradient over the whole
screen at 45 %, which updated 1001 x 609 px of the panel to show a menu of
about 200 x 330 px.

The panel is now white with the e-paper outline and corner radius
(docs/design/eink-ui.md, rule 3; SystemUI's values in res/values/pw3_eink.xml),
and the window has no background, so only the panel is drawn.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/pw3_global_actions_bg.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- PW3: the power menu's panel is white with an outline, as everything that floats above
+     the page (docs/design/eink-ui.md, rule 3): SystemUI is drawn in software, where its
+     elevation casts no shadow. -->
+<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
+       android:shape="rectangle">
+    <solid android:color="@android:color/white" />
+    <stroke android:width="@dimen/pw3_outline_width" android:color="@color/pw3_outline" />
+    <corners android:radius="@dimen/pw3_corner_radius" />
+</shape>
